csv-reader-drop-in
==================

This entry is a faster drop-in for make.fun's csv-reader 1.0.0, the reference
program of the csv-reader-speed-01-run-20261121 competition. Its reading policy
— the broken-row rules it reproduces exactly — is csv-reader's own, and this
entry claims no authorship of that policy: it is a re-implementation of
csv-reader 1.0.0's documented behaviour, written for speed.

csv-reader 1.0.0 is make.fun's own code (MIT), itself derived from:

- d3-dsv 3.0.2 (ISC, https://github.com/d3/d3-dsv), whose parseRows loop
  csv-reader's token walk follows;
- papaparse 5.7.1 (MIT, https://github.com/mholt/PapaParse), whose errors
  array idea csv-reader's error records follow.

The upstream licences, copyright lines and source links are carried in the
competition kit's baseline (baseline/csv-reader/vendor/csv-reader/), with its
LICENSE and NOTICE word for word.
